      {
        "id": 88349,
        "name": "Envisioner",
        "username": "Envisioner",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-16T21:44:11.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I really like the idea of a villain deck that represents an entire organization rather than a person, with the character card never being a target but offering an alternate win condition a la Gloomweaver, which is the ONLY way to win instead of letting you just beat him up most games.&nbsp; I'm thinking it'd be most appropriate for the company founded by Michael Conteh before he became The Naturalist, and to be Natch's nemesis, but that doesn't necessarily mean it can't also be Revocorp, or have been bought out by them.&nbsp; (Perhaps Equity was the CEO after Mr. Conteh, and lost his job when RevoCorp bought the company out after its profits dropped due to Michael's disappearance, so when he somehow found out Natch was Conteh, he swore to punish him before turning his vengeful attention to Revenant?&nbsp; I forget whenther Equity and Revenant are in the same or different Vengeance decks; either way, perhaps they hate each other but are temporarily working together).</p>",
        "post_number": 22,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:12:58.518Z",
