        "name": "Craig",
        "username": "Craig",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/craig/{size}/2150_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-21T10:45:22.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"bessyrocks12\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bessyrocks12/48/2447_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> bessyrocks12:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Maybe this is a crazy idea, but could there be a new mechanic that combines the environment and villain deck into a unified opponent. Like the Chairman and Rook City work well together, but actually having mechanics in each that makes the combination more difficult. Additional effects against hero characters exists within the nemeses cards of Vengeance, but why couldn't an environment and villain have effect cards that improve each. RevoCorp seems like an ideal setting/villain.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Long ago, we discussed the idea of a villain that was the environment. Like a giant space amoeba that the heroes were fighting from the inside, or something to that effect. I still think it's a neat idea.</p>",
