      {
        "id": 88358,
        "name": "cmschex",
        "username": "cmschex",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/e9bcb4/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-21T19:06:07.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"McBehrer\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mcbehrer/48/1850_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> McBehrer:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Yeah, looking at the final version of the cards (higher resolution than my printed-out proofs) it definitely looks tech, rather than alien. I actually kind of see him as a Green Goblin analogue to Setback's Peter Parker, with RevoCorp being the Sentinels universe's OsCorp (it even has the same name formatting!) Plus with RevoCorp's tendency to experiment on dangerous/volatile technology (Omnitron's code), and the sudden appearence of a Sinister-Six-esque group of villains (in the Amazing Spider-Man movies it looks like OsCorp is directly responsible for the Lizard, Goblin, Rhino, Vulture, and Octopus, at least) and the connection's pretty strong.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I think this is totally on point, especially considering the image on Wrong Time and Place, which seems very much an homage to Amazing Spider Man <span class=\"hashtag-raw\">#122</span> where Spidey ducks as Green Goblin gets impaled by his own glider. &nbsp;</p>",
